    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1035">

                <pb facs="1141" n="1045" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1045"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Polo de Bernabé
                        to Mr. Sherman</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain in Washington</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April 2,
                                1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 33.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor, by order of my
                    Government, to transmit to your excellency the full testimony<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d1035-f1"/> in the inquiry instituted by the maritime authority of
                    the Habana station by reason of the catastrophe which befell the U. S. ironclad
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> in that port, in <pb facs="1142" n="1046"
                        xml:id="pg1046"/> the night of the 15th of February last, which awful
                    misfortune to the American people has been so deeply and sincerely lamented by
                    the Spanish Government and people.</p>
                <p>I improve this opportunity, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Polo de Bernabé.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1035-f1" n="3" xml:id="d1035-f1-content">
                <p>The full report is published in Senate Report No. 885, Fifty-fifth Congress,
                    second session.</p>
            </note>
